<urn:atm:triage:finding/FNX-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FNX-004" ;
  triage:title "Heartbeat-originated attention dispatch is an untracked, undrained detached tokio::spawn task" ;
  triage:description "fenix's independent critical review of PR #1395 confirms the CDR-002 fix itself is real and well tested (IdleOpportunitySink installed on the router, heartbeat publishes post-commit for every accepted Idle revision including Idle-to-Idle, composed tests drive the real pump with no Herdr poll). The delivery mechanism is the gap: HerdrQueueWakePump::on_idle_opportunity does tokio::spawn(async move { ... }) with no retained JoinHandle, no RuntimeHealth counter, and nothing checking draining state; each call gets a fresh HerdrQueueWakeStats so HERDR_MAX_PROMPTS_PER_TICK no longer bounds prompt volume on this path. The router already owns the answer to this exact shape: DetachedReceivedHooks (router_support.rs:315-364), whose doc states 'never unobserved: every warning it produces is logged with the originating request id and counted on RuntimeHealth, and daemon shutdown drains whatever is still in flight instead of abandoning it mid-emission', with a bounded drain(deadline). Concrete consequence: during drain, heartbeats still arriving start brand-new nudge dispatches that nothing waits for. Recommendation: route heartbeat-originated dispatch through DetachedReceivedHooks (or an equivalent registry on the pump), add a RuntimeHealth counter, and skip publication when the runtime is draining. Add a test that a drain joins an in-flight heartbeat-originated dispatch." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "lifecycle-management" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-10T20:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "arch-ctm" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-10T19:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AZ.4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-10T19:42:59Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FNX-004/AZ4-001> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

